# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/agentsview/ is gitignored.
#
# TOOLCHAIN SOURCE — a tool this repo actually RUNS.
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: the agentsview binary itself (`agentsview --version`)
#   pinned here:    0.42.0
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS NOW. `mise.toml` refused a manifest on 2026-09-01 with a
# stated, conditional reason: "`kb-build` is currently FAILING and `graph-size`
# sits at 736 MiB of 1,024". BOTH CONDITIONS HAVE MOVED — measured 2026-09-11:
# kb-build is green at 472,069 nodes, and graph-size is 721.2 MiB of 1,024
# (70%, 303 MiB headroom, rc 0). A refusal that carried its condition is a
# refusal that can be re-decided when the condition changes, which is the whole
# reason the original note wrote the numbers down.
#
# ⚠️ THE PIN IS A RELEASE BEHIND THE FEATURE WE WANT. `effort` capture for
# Claude Code AND Codex sessions is upstream PR #1677, merged 2026-09-10 and in
# NO RELEASE YET. v0.42.0 (2026-09-01) does not carry it. When the release that
# does lands — do NOT assume it is v0.43.0 — bumping triggers a documented FULL
# SESSION RESYNC to populate effort from source transcripts, which against a
# ~5 GB archive is a real cost, not a formality.
#
# The tag is ANNOTATED, so `commit` below is the PEELED commit, not the tag
# object `94b3676f3cfcb32d95ff07547db727e3c95564ba`. Recording the tag object
# would pin a thing that is not a tree.

